.TH PATHALLELE 1 "2026-11-10" "PathAllele 0.2.0-dev.20261110" "Bioinformatics tools"
.SH NAME
pathallele \- haploid variant calling from assembled graph paths
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pathallele
.BI -g " graph.gfa"
.BI -r " reference.fa"
.BI -o " directory"
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
PathAllele resolves physical sequence occurrences in haploid assembly paths,
calls complete local alleles and projects exact events to the reference.
Graph homology is combined with separately bounded minimap2 alignment
components
and unique exact sequence anchors. Ambiguous copies, unbounded junctions and
unresolved sequence are retained as missing observations.
.PP
An independently bounded local call may remain resolved inside broader
uncertain
structure only when one source chain covers the interval and both flanks.
Adjacent chains are not joined to satisfy this requirement.
.PP
Calling uses the built-in vcflib/WFA2 backend. Native shared libraries are
installed by the package manager; no external alignment executable is required.
The native-aligner build feature is required for calling.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "-g, --graph " FILE
GFA1 with explicit IUPAC segment sequences, P paths and 0M links. All graph
paths
are validated, including paths outside the selected cohort.
.TP
.BI "-r, --reference " FILE
One A/C/G/T FASTA sequence matching one complete graph path.
.TP
.BI "-s, --samples " FILE
Optional non-reference haploid sample subset/order, one ID per line.
Without this option, select all non-reference samples in first-path order
(first-row order with --path-map). Multiple contigs per sample are allowed;
multiple haplotypes per sample are not.
.TP
.BI "-o, --output " DIR
New output directory. Existing results are not overwritten.
.TP
.BI --path-map " FILE"
Tab-delimited path-to-sample map with a header containing path and sample.
Default: sample#haplotype#contig (PanSN) path names.
.TP
.BI --reference-path " STR"
Explicit reference GFA path. Default: infer from the reference sequence.
.TP
.B --resume
Resume only when input, executable, dependency and option identities match.
The original work directory is required. A completed run is hash-checked.
.TP
.BI "-t, --threads " INT
Mapping, source-processing and compression worker threads [16].
.TP
.BI "-j, --jobs " INT
Concurrent external allele-alignment jobs [8].
.TP
.BI --minimum-anchor " INT"
Minimum source/graph homology anchor length in bp; at least 19 [31].
.TP
.BI "-k, --mapping-k " INT
Minimap2 and fallback exact-seed k-mer length; at least 19 [19].
.TP
.BI --maximum-graph-gap " INT"
Maximum graph-context anchor chaining gap in bp [1000].
.TP
.BI --sequence-anchor " INT"
Exact-sequence anchor length within source alleles in bp; at least 19 [31].
.TP
.BI "-q, --minimum-mapq " INT
Minimum source-alignment MAPQ, from 0 to 60 [20].
.TP
.BI --max-matrix-gb " FLOAT"
Numeric genotype row-buffer budget in GiB [8]. This is not a process memory
limit; graph and source models require additional memory.
.TP
.BI --mapping-batch-bases " INT"
Minimap2 query mini-batch size in bases [50000000].
.TP
.BI --mapping-cache-bytes " INT"
Release minimap2 per-thread cache above this many bytes; zero disables release
[50000000].
.SH FILE FORMATS
VCF positions are 1-based. TSV intervals are 0-based and half-open.
All VCF genotypes are haploid; a dot denotes missing data.
.TP
.B Graph.vcf.gz
Exact event projection. GT indexes this record's REF/ALT; FT records why a
genotype is missing. GT=0 is an event backbone, which can contain changes
represented at other linked records. AC/AN/AF exclude missing calls.
.TP
.B Graph.loci.vcf.gz
All complete loci, including reference-only records. GT/FT describe the
observed
complete sequence and source status; PG/PF describe its event projection.
GT and PG index Graph.loci.tsv.gz, not the event VCF ALT order.
Overlapping loci are separate sequence views and cannot all be replayed as
independent edits on one reference.
.TP
.B Graph.loci.tsv.gz
Complete sequence dictionary indexed by locus_id and allele_index; index 0 is
REF.
.TP
.B Graph.variant_annotations.tsv.gz
Unified allele classification and exact inversion sequence witnesses.
.TP
.B Graph.sv.vcf.gz
Symbolic structural groups. GT is 1 for presence, 0 for supported absence or a
dot for insufficient/conflicting evidence; FT records source status. Exact
member sequences are retained in the complete catalogue.
.TP
.B Graph.sv_members.tsv.gz
Maps structure_id to locus_id, complete allele_index and event_allele_index.
SEED rows are emitted SV alleles; COMPLETE rows are additional compatible
complete alleles. Event indexes can be absent for COMPLETE members.
.TP
.B Graph.paths.tsv.gz, Graph.alleles.tsv.gz, Graph.anchors.tsv.gz
Physical source occurrences, allele sequences and homology anchors.
Graph.nodes.tsv.gz maps signed internal handles to original GFA segment IDs.
.TP
.B Graph.projection_links.tsv.gz
Component records supporting a complete allele's event projection.
.TP
.B run.json, schema.json
Input/tool SHA256 identities, execution metrics, resume identities and output schema.
Work checkpoints are private versioned data, not an interchange format.
.SH CLASSIFICATION AND STRUCTURAL GROUPS
TYPE distinguishes SNV, MNV, INS, DEL, REPLACEMENT, INV, INV_COMPLEX and
COMPLEX.
SEQTYPE records sequence shape independently. REPLACEMENT has nonempty,
unequal-length REF and ALT edits. SIZECLASS is SV when the larger trimmed
allele
is at least 50 bp. INV requires an exact same-interval reverse complement;
INV_COMPLEX retains an inverted component with additional changes or shifted
boundaries. Sequence-only inversion evidence requires a unique informative
reverse core of at least 31 bp. These labels do not determine mutation
history.
.PP
Structural groups are seeded from emitted SV alleles without using phenotype
or
frequency. Deterministic complete-link clustering requires compatible classes
and inversion axes, endpoint distances at most 5% of the shorter span (bounded
to 1-50 bp), and at least 95% reference-span, ALT-length and sequence
similarity.
Sequences are compared in a common reference frame; deletions compare deleted
sequence. Approximate non-deletion groups must be separated from the reference
background beyond the same distance budget. Insertions at different positions
are not merged without a closed common frame. COMPLEX receives exact
deduplication only. An additional complete allele must uniquely match every
member of the group.
.PP
Structural absence uses a complete member locus covering the group's envelope,
never projected event GT=0 alone. Conflicting positive and negative evidence
remains missing. Groups are statistical analysis units, not ancestral events.
.SH LIMITATIONS
One linear reference and haploid assembly paths are supported.
Diploid/polyploid
calling, W walks, overlapping segments and circular reference coordinates are
not supported. Memory grows with graph size and sample count. Some inversions
with additional sequence changes remain unresolved upstream. Validation checks
implemented source-consistency contracts; it does not establish whole-genome
completeness or independent biological sensitivity and specificity.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; two for invalid input, sequence consistency failures or execution errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR minimap2 (1),
.BR bcftools (1),
.BR samtools (1)
